     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a>: the wiki page with better information for setting up Camel is:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Setup+Camel+Message+Integrations\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Setup+Camel+Message+Integrations</a></p>\n\n<p>That page has info on setting up Karaf, as well as deploying Camel packages to a servlet container.  So that seems like the best documentation to follow for the vagrant work, though we'll need to update it with the newly-added header info too.</p>",
